## Why hold telemetry, not an initial report run lock

scoped_reports230/398–399 drops the initial PathTx on output refusal, then
scoped_output_refusal32 reacquires a full RunTx. Queueing a drain behind the
initial path report does not force report commit first. Instead block the actual
refusal's root telemetry upsert while it ALREADY owns the run: refusal86–101 /
PGexecution4230–4249. No telemetry row is inserted/updated by fixture SQL.

Before concurrency, existing migration/source/authority checks, normal Keeper
renewal, original live uncancelled c10[0]/reserve, scopeOPEN/no stop/failure/Return/
free slot and E4200020. Require zero selected-run chain membership. Capture v0,
complete existing execution footprint and telemetry row head=v0.
Create separate role-correct max1 PgRunStore scheduler pool, fresh cache and same
real Keeper placement; capture backendPID S/database/current_user/backend_start.
Set native S PoolConfig statement_timeout30s/idle_transaction60s. For CAS only,
existing TestApi Options.statement_timeout=30s configures the actual API pool;
keep Direct10s default untouched. Keep pools alive and identities verified. All
participants use owner or sagat_app URLs derived from the exact owned fixture.
No permissions are widened. Before launching reportR, acquire/pin observerO from
API pool; validate role/database/PID/backend_start, O!=S and retain O through
cleanup. Each observation executes on O in autocommit, never a new pool checkout.
Later require O!=H/R/S. Thus cleanup never reuses R to observe its own active
transaction. API pool has8 connections; O is independent of reporting R.
Initialize Metrics::global before race; capture relevant existing counters.

## Two observed blocking edges and actual typed CAS

Create dedicated owner holder pool max1 with PoolConfig statement_timeout30s,
idle_transaction60s/acquire3s. Capture verifiedH/database/user/backend_start before
BEGIN; use existing BeginSafely under bounded acquisition (never timed raw begin),
recheck same identity in returned tx, then bounded keyed telemetry FOR UPDATE.
No lock is held before identity checks. O/H/S distinct before report launch. Send unchanged retained original complete_step via a
cloned current authenticated client, retaining its JoinHandle. No new worker,
registration, poll, key, renewal, rebuilt report or capability edit.
Observe exactly one actual API-role report backend R active/Lock at native
telemetry upsert and blocked byH. Use fresh autocommit observer queries through
API-role pool (same role sessions visible); match db/user/queryshape/PID/edges,
not generic lock counts or whole session dumps. Report actor remains held there.
Committed full footprint must still equal prestate; uncommitted stop is invisible.

Launch actual public scheduler.advance_collection using dedicated actorS. Its
read-only repeatable-read frontier sees old v0/no stop/E; native start-drain then
blocks on run owned byR. Require S active/Lock at EXACT native drain SQL selecting
namespace_id,workflow_version_id,run_version,status,stop_reason,stop_code,paused
FROM runs ... FOR UPDATE (primitives648–684). A full-run fallback waits at a
different query and is a failure. Recheck both H→R and R→S blocking edges together,
known actors/databases/roles/queryshapes and unchanged committed footprint.

Only after both edges, ROLLBACK holder. Join actual report and scheduler under
bounded deadlines. Report must deliver accepted original SUCCEEDED/CANCELLING ACK.
Scheduler MUST return CollectionAdvanceError::Primitive(PrimitiveStoreError::
RevisionConflict{current:v1}); no retry/fallback, Waiting/Skipped/arbitrary error.
v1>v0 and v1 equals independently persisted head, receipt revision and ACK revision.
Native drain checks revision before evidence/mutation (primitives2494/687–696);
public advance propagates it (passes1830–1837), while tick would hide it asSkipped.

