## Bounded error cleanup is part of proof

Use5s per blocking-edge observation,3s bounded proof queries and bounded actor
joins inside existing300s phase;90s cooperative scenario budget is NEW and must not cancel cleanup. Actor statement30s
exceeds the combined happy-path observation budget; idle timeout60s bounds held
tx. Use timeout+yield_now barrier pattern, no sleeps. PinnedO autocommit stats
queries avoid both snapshot caching and self-observation.
Never assert/panic while holder is retained: collect proof Result, rollback holder
on every path, then surface errors only AFTER actor cleanup. Bound holder
rollback5s. If rollback fails/times out, acceptance fails: close holder pool and
use independent bounded owner cleanup connection to terminate ONLY verified
holder identity (PID+database+user+backend_start all match). Verify original H
session absent, or idle with no transaction after successful rollback, before
joining blocked actors. H status is ALWAYS read through an independent OWNER
cleanup connection (runtimeO cannot see owner transaction fields). Same-identity predicate prevents PID-reuse termination.
Do not infer lock release from drop, timeout or TestApi::drop alone. Existing witness
helpers that panic must run in an owned joined task or equivalent capture so an
unexpected read failure still releases holder. Keep all actor handles; aborting
a client alone does not prove the server stopped. After rollback, bounded-join
both actors, verify their server transactions are closed, then close dedicated
H/S pools. PinnedO observes only same-role R/S; release O after those checks and
BEFORE any main API-pool close. On the happy path main API stays open for the
accepted lifecycle. TestApi drop never replaces these verified close/join steps. If cleanup requires cancelling a known actor backend, use only identified
owned PID after barrier release, record failure, and never count it as CAS success.
On failure before reportPID identification, release holder first and ensure
bounded API/server/pool closure and verified actor server-state cleanup; retain
safe evidence, no loose actors. TestApi::drop only aborts private server handles,
so it is not the cleanup proof: actor joins/pool closures plus pinnedO backend
checks are required. Any emergency actor cancellation/termination uses the same
verified identity predicate and makes the test fail; it never proves CAS success.
No sql state/status/lease/receipt/output edits, sleeps, alternate success or retry
on mutated handoff. Real timeout/query/error/cleanup failure stops acceptance.

## Sources and root gates

PG16 READ COMMITTED may lock the row version committed by a concurrent updater;
separate read-only frontier retains its own earlier snapshot. Root verified
[isolation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/transaction-iso.html).
Use fresh stats reads, observing only sessions of the participant role; root
verified [visibility/snapshots](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/monitoring-stats.html).
Blocking PIDs can include earlier incompatible waiters, so query and both edges
are required; root verified [blocking semantics](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/functions-info.html).

